 "asked_at": "2026-10-17T16:45+08:00",
 "answer": "The latest reading I found puts Shah Alam's API at **168 (Unhealthy)** as of 5:30 pm today, according to a Bernama report using the Department of Environment's APIMS data.\n\nThis is the newest figure I could find, not a live one. APIMS updates every hour, so the number may have changed since.\n\n**Other Selangor readings in the same update:** Johan Setia 184, Klang 176, Petaling Jaya 173, Banting 162 and Kuala Selangor 152. Two places in Johor, Larkin and Pasir Gudang, reached 202, which counts as Very Unhealthy.\n\n**What the API numbers mean:**\n- 0–50: Good\n- 51–100: Moderate\n- 101–200: Unhealthy\n- 201–300: Very Unhealthy\n- Above 300: Hazardous\n\n**Trend:** Shah Alam was at 180 yesterday at 5 pm, so today is slightly better, but the air is still unhealthy because of the haze. If you can, stay indoors, keep outdoor exercise to a minimum, and wear an N95 mask if you have to go out. This matters most for children, older people and anyone with breathing problems.\n\nFor the current hourly reading, check the APIMS portal (eqms.doe.gov.my) or the MyIPU app.",
